/*  walkRefT -- R2's certificate row, and it REFUSED R2. C-160 stroke 2, 2026-09-04.

    A bare accessor DIRECTLY inside a ++ walk, with NO intervening call, so
    nothing but the walk writer can have aimed lastREF at the read. addrOf beside
    it, so the claim is identity and not just a string.

    PRE-REGISTERED: flip reads the CURSOR HOLDER's name before R2 and the
    member's after; bare reads the member both times.

    MEASURED, both arms, before any R2 edit:

      arm FLIP : aa   bb   wrHeld     addrOf(wrCur) = one stable node, #1/#2
      arm BARE : aa   bb   wrTarget   same walk, same members

    TWO FINDINGS, and together they are why R2 did not land.

    1. THE PRE-REGISTRATION IS FALSIFIED. With no intervening call the flip
       already reads the MEMBER, not the cursor holder. lastREF holds the member
       on both arms -- which is what C-158's LastRefWriters recon said in the
       first place: every writer stores the HELD. So R2s premise, that the walk
       writers store the cursor FIELD, does not hold at any of the four sites.
       shadowCensus never showed otherwise: its defect was the INTERVENING CALL,
       closed by R1s capture-then-call and by C-160s scDcol(*scCur).

    2. THE ARMS ALREADY DISAGREE ON A HOLDER MEMBER, AND BARE IS THE ONE DOING
       WHAT R2 PROPOSES. wrHeld is a member that is itself a holder. Bare reads
       wrTarget -- it follows the holder level, because the bare road auto-
       unwraps. The flip reads wrHeld -- the members own identity, preserved.
       R2 would follow one holder level at the write, which makes the FLIP
       behave like BARE here: it would re-introduce, for lastREF, exactly the
       auto-unwrap the flip exists to remove. On a case that is currently
       correct under the flip.

    So R2 is not a no-op and not a fix; it is a behaviour change on holder
    members, in the direction the flip is travelling away from. Reported and
    held, per the stop clause. This fixture is the evidence and stays.  */

register(WalkRefT);
define
    wrBag aa bb;
    wrTarget="TGT";
    wrHeld;
    wrRun code={
        wrHeld := wrTarget;
        wrBag +% wrHeld;
        iterate wrCur attributes on wrBag;
        while ++wrCur;
            cerr "W bare taG =" taG " <- member name; R2 would change a HOLDER member to its target":;
            addrOf(wrCur);
        };
    ;
wrRun();
print "WALKREFT SENTINEL":;
stop();
